  - TOV21G: MMR-PANEL HIT — REPORT, DO NOT OMIT: EPCAM p.2_3fs (Frame_Shift_Ins). EPCAM is on this panel as an INDIRECT MMR mechanism (3'-end deletions silence MSH2 in cis); this call is a 5' frameshift near the start codon, which truncates EPCAM itself and does NOT invoke that mechanism. TUMOUR-ONLY WES, no matched normal => GERMLINE CANNOT BE EXCLUDED (EPCAM/Lynch germline deletions exist). The variant is novel in dbSNP, carries no VAF support (indel representations do not join the VCF), and sits in the panel's one hypermutator, where passenger risk is elevated. Requires MMR IHC / MSI-PCR and germline testing before any mechanistic claim.
  - TOV2881EP: MMR-PANEL HIT — secondary/proofreading gene: MSH3 p.Y334F [Missense_Mutation; VAF 0.649; ClinVar uncertain_significance]. Tumour-only WES => germline cannot be excluded; not an established MMR-loss mechanism on its own.
